title:: CaosInstrument
summary:: A track voice: SynthDef or function, route, params and note line.
categories:: CaosBox
related:: Classes/CaosGear, Classes/CaosTrack

description::
A CaosInstrument knows how to sound (SynthDef or function), where it goes out
(code::out::), with which parameters (code::params::) and, if melodic, how its
note line advances. It does not know about the GUI or the clock: it receives
code::trigger::, code::set::, code::release:: and code::free::.

list::
## code::kind:: — code::\synth:: or code::\function::.
## code::mode:: — code::\free:: advances with the clock; code::\trig:: advances on trigger.
## code::retrigger:: — a new voice per trigger, or legato.
## code::oneShot:: — percussive envelopes with no live node to release.
::

instancemethods::

method:: trigger
method:: retriggerCurrent
Repeats the current note and SynthDef with a new voice, without advancing the
note or the chord sequence. It is what the step repeater uses internally.
method:: noteOn
method:: noteOff
method:: isHeld
Play a note from a MIDI keyboard on the same voice. code::noteOn(note,
velocity):: sets code::note::, triggers a voice and scales the code::amp::
arguments by the velocity for that note only. code::noteOff(note):: clears
code::liveNote:: when it is the held key; one-shot voices keep their envelope
tail, gated voices receive gate 0. The sequence is not frozen: the next
code::advance:: returns to the note line.
code::
i.noteOn(60, 100);
i.noteOff(60);
i.isHeld; // false
::
method:: set
method:: out
code::
i = CaosGear.new.bass(50);
i.out_(\master);
i.set(\cutf, 1200);
i.trigger;
i.release;
::

method:: updateTimbre
Changes the SynthDef variant of a melodic instrument without creating a new
instrument. The current voice is released; notes, params, route, mode,
retrigger and oneShot are preserved. The next trigger uses the new variant.
A manual chord change also stops any automatic chord sequence; re-declare the
instrument with code::chordsArray::/code::seqType:: to start a new sequence.

Named arguments:
list::
## code::waveform::: for code::pad:: only. Must be one of
   code::CaosGear.waveforms::.
## code::chord::: for code::chords:: or code::chords2:: only. Must be one of
   code::CaosGear.validChords(\chords):: or
   code::CaosGear.validChords(\chords2)::.
## first positional argument: any SynthDef name, for advanced use.
::

code::
g = CaosGear.new;

p = g.pad(waveform: 'sin');
p.updateTimbre(waveform: 'tri');

c = g.chords(chordsArray: #['m']);
c.updateTimbre(chord: 'M7');

c2 = g.chords2(chordsArray: #['M']);
c2.updateTimbre(chord: 'M9');

// escape hatch: use a loaded SynthDef directly
p.updateTimbre(\ambuno_pulse);
::

note:: An invalid waveform or chord leaves the current timbre unchanged and posts
a warning. code::set(\chord, ...):: still does not change the SynthDef; use
code::updateTimbre:: for that.
::
